                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d1229ae8-f1bc-3359-b926-333afad806bf",
                        "entry_id": "2a7f6d0f-ee9e-363b-838f-6bccfb141bee",
                        "glosses": [
                            "матем. многочлен, комбинирующий элементы квадратной матрицы таким образом, что его значение сохраняется при транспонировании и линейных комбинациях строк или столбцов"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e732657f-4be9-3200-8dfe-7be8b332ec52",
                        "entry_id": "2a7f6d0f-ee9e-363b-838f-6bccfb141bee",
                        "glosses": [
                            "справочник по видам"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7f3f0412-88f2-4d67-9449-a0bc47356265",
                                "sense_id": "e732657f-4be9-3200-8dfe-7be8b332ec52",
                                "text": "Уже тяжело больной, Виталий Валентинович начинает писать две ранее задуманные книги ― художественно-поэтический определитель птиц и раздумья о литературном труде."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3183b755-fd96-32d6-8109-a225710e8b48",
                        "entry_id": "2a7f6d0f-ee9e-363b-838f-6bccfb141bee",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. то же, что определитель номера"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "04fb2052-9897-417e-9016-423312d5ac21",
                                "sense_id": "3183b755-fd96-32d6-8109-a225710e8b48",
                                "text": "Я вытащила свой телефон и посмотрела на определитель."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c116d77d-c43a-4d68-8d80-50fbd3f5a5b4",
                        "source_entry_id": "2a7f6d0f-ee9e-363b-838f-6bccfb141bee",
                        "source_sense_description": "детерминант",
                        "target_lang_word": "determinant",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "determinant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0a9c9b0a-e789-3111-962f-467242a99339",
                                        "entry_id": "67081d94-9ec3-3faf-be19-949cd661d6d6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A determining factor; an element that determines the nature of something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16a096d8-10ca-4b13-885c-a4635945f602",
                                                "sense_id": "0a9c9b0a-e789-3111-962f-467242a99339",
                                                "text": "1999, Noah P. Barsky, Stuart Bruchey (editor), Organizational Determinants of Budgetary Influence and Involvement, Taylor & Francis (Garland Publishing), page 4,\nShields and Young (1993) argue that the budget participation literature \"has not produced a coherent nor unified definition\" of both the determinants and consequences of budget participation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2106a20-c4c7-4956-954e-a326a2f3a3a2",
                                                "sense_id": "0a9c9b0a-e789-3111-962f-467242a99339",
                                                "text": "The field of the social determinants of health is perhaps the most complex and challenging of all."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8cb95315-364e-4a1b-a831-b880d42ce8d6",
                                                "sense_id": "0a9c9b0a-e789-3111-962f-467242a99339",
                                                "text": "The aim of this book has been to assess the determinants of capital punishment without taking a stand for or against the death penalty."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "85601563-5000-3dd9-a6b4-e8894e8b29e6",
                                        "entry_id": "67081d94-9ec3-3faf-be19-949cd661d6d6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A scalar that encodes certain characteristics of a given transformation matrix; the unique scalar function over square matrices which is distributive over matrix multiplication, multilinear in the rows and columns, and takes the value 1 for the unit matrix; abbreviated as: det."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92eda765-3153-4f8e-bb58-bbae3ef4fa14",
                                                "sense_id": "85601563-5000-3dd9-a6b4-e8894e8b29e6",
                                                "text": "1966 [Allyn & Bacon], Howard Whitley Eves, Elementary Matrix Theory, 1980, Dover, Unabridged corrected republication, page 165,\nThe determinant of a square matrix A_(n) is a function (actually a polynomial function) of the elements a_ij of A."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c646c848-abd7-4d18-8d33-f048dd58c472",
                                                "sense_id": "85601563-5000-3dd9-a6b4-e8894e8b29e6",
                                                "text": "1990, Assem S. Deif, Advanced Matrix Theory for Scientists and Engineers, Gordon and Breach Science Publishers (Abacus Press), 2nd Edition, page 18,\nShow that the determinant of a Hermitian matrix is real and that of a skew-Hermitian matrix is imaginary."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "30508342-53ee-4f2a-91d7-584cc727c45a",
                                                "sense_id": "85601563-5000-3dd9-a6b4-e8894e8b29e6",
                                                "text": "Using this definition, we derive the basic properties of a determinant that are useful in its evaluation. In particular, it is shown how the calculation of a determinant can be reduced to the calculation of determinants of lower order."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ad54700-02f9-428c-90de-31ecbd3d8f92",
                                                "sense_id": "85601563-5000-3dd9-a6b4-e8894e8b29e6",
                                                "text": "The following proposition shows a connection between negafibonacci numbers and the determinants of a family of tridiagonal matrices. […] Assuming that the determinant det(Gₖ) = f₋₍ₖ₊₁₎ for all k ≤ n, we aim to show that det(Gₙ₊₂) = f₋₍ₙ₊₃₎."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1397e9d9-7d71-301c-a969-90bc3a816321",
                                        "entry_id": "67081d94-9ec3-3faf-be19-949cd661d6d6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A substance that causes a cell to adopt a particular fate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "92e5d3a0-abc7-300a-b562-42c47d6ab458",
                                        "entry_id": "67081d94-9ec3-3faf-be19-949cd661d6d6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something that causes a nuclease to cut at a specified point"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "determinant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6ddae74d-8509-30c8-923c-45ecb740027a",
                                        "entry_id": "2827ad4d-7e49-359a-bfa0-a6abfcf43abe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Serving to determine or limit; determinative."
                                        ],
